var MH_CHK_NOTES_SECURITY='Only Alex may read or write these notes. Make one security role for this table (for example "Manager notes") with Create, Read and Write at Organization level, and no Delete (the hub never deletes a note: Remove marks it Removed). Give that role to Alex and to nobody else, and do not add this table to any other role. Then switch on auditing for the table (its Properties, Advanced options, Audit changes to its data; auditing must also be on for the environment), so every change is recorded. Two built-in roles reach this table anyway: System Administrator can always read every row, and System Customizer gets full access to new custom tables by default. Open the System Customizer role and set the notes table (display name Employee note, or _m_Employee note if yours is craa5__m_employeenote) to None (or User level), and check who holds System Administrator in this environment.';// One column of the list. extra: primary, maxLength, min, max, options, optionValues, optionsNote, guess (the type is not confirmed:
